# Tutorial 13 — Camera and Staging
# [camera pan], [camera zoom], multi-character blocking, and visual composition.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_13_camera_staging
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1650]
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]
Lavender: Tutorial 03 covered where characters stand. This tutorial covers where the {b}camera{/b} looks and how to stage scenes with intention.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Two commands: {b}[camera pan]{/b} and {b}[camera zoom]{/b}. Plus staging principles.

@label lesson_menu
[show lavender far_left talking]
> [camera pan] — moving the viewport -> section_pan
> [camera zoom] — close-ups and wide shots -> section_zoom
> Staging two characters -> section_two_char
> Composition principles -> section_composition
> Quick reference: staging commands -> quick_reference
